scenarios.text:
A car park has a single-lane ramp. Cars may use it in one direction at a time (up or down), with at most 4 cars on it at once. The controller uses POSIX semaphores:

```c
sem_t ramp;          /* 1 : the ramp belongs to one direction             */
sem_t cap;           /* 4 : places on the ramp                            */
sem_t mutex_up;      /* 1 : protects n_up                                 */
sem_t mutex_down;    /* 1 : protects n_down                               */
int n_up = 0, n_down = 0;

void go_up(int id) {
    sem_wait(&mutex_up);
    if (++n_up == 1) sem_wait(&ramp);   /* first car up claims the ramp     */
    sem_post(&mutex_up);

    sem_wait(&cap);  drive_up(id);  sem_post(&cap);

    sem_wait(&mutex_up);
    if (--n_up == 0) sem_post(&ramp);   /* last car up releases it          */
    sem_post(&mutex_up);
}
/* go_down() is the same with n_down and mutex_down */
```

At closing time 5 attendants each count the cars on one floor; nobody may start the next round of counting until all 5 have finished the current round. A colleague builds this barrier from one counter and one semaphore.

